; Return in the main program: it goes back to the last Gosub, and with no Gosub left to go back to it ends the program like End,
; as in the original (which leaves the main program there). Goto-loops with a Gosub label behind them are written like this.
Include "check.bb"

Global hits = 0
Gosub count
Gosub count
Check "Return goes back to the Gosub", hits, 2
